# Environment Variables Example
#
# IMPORTANT: This file is committed to version control and documents
# required variables and their purposes.
#
# NEVER include actual credentials, tokens, or secrets in this file.
# NEVER commit your .env file (containing real values) to version control.
#
# Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file: cp .env.example .env
# 2. Edit .env and fill in your actual values (not shared with repo)
# 3. Add .env to .gitignore (it should already be there)
# 4. Load variables before running the app: source .env

# ─── Continuous Integration & Code Quality ───────────────────────────

# Codecov Token (for coverage reports in CI)
# Get from: https://app.codecov.io/account/settings
CODECOV_TOKEN=

# GitHub Token (automatically provided in Actions, but useful for local tools)
# Create: https://github.com/settings/tokens (requires repo scope)
# GitHub Actions provides GITHUB_TOKEN automatically - no setup needed
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ─── AI & LLM APIs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OpenAI API Key (if using AI agents locally)
# Get from: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Anthropic API Key (if using Claude API)
# Get from: https://console.anthropic.com/
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ─── Database & Configuration ─────────────────────────────────────────

# Database URL (if applicable)
# Format: postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/dbname
# Note: Use environment variable for credentials, NOT hardcoded in code
# DATABASE_URL=

# Debug Mode (optional)
# DEBUG=false

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SECURITY REMINDER:
#
# ✓ DO: Store secrets in environment variables
# ✓ DO: Use .env files for local development
# ✓ DO: Add .env to .gitignore
# ✓ DO: Use a secret manager for production
# ✓ DO: Rotate credentials regularly
#
# ✗ DON'T: Hardcode secrets in source code
# ✗ DON'T: Commit .env files to version control
# ✗ DON'T: Log or print secret values
#
# If you accidentally commit a secret:
# 1. Rotate the credential immediately
# 2. Use BFG Repo Cleaner: https://rtyley.github.io/bfg-repo-cleaner/
# 3. Force-push to remove from remote
